<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
    <Document>
        <name>Wasatch Mountains West -- Deer Scouting Map</name>
        <description>Wasatch Mountains West -- deer scouting map, built from real DWR data

WHAT'S IN HERE:
1. Unit Boundary -- traced from the official DWR legal description (I-80/US-40/
   Strawberry Bay Marina Rd/USFS 042/USFS 051/US-6/I-15), not surveyed parcel data.
2. DWR Mule Deer Crucial Habitat -- REAL Utah DWR data (Utah Mule Deer Habitat
   dataset), clipped to this unit. Colored by season. This is actual DWR-mapped
   habitat, not a derived/guessed layer.
3. Wilderness Areas (foot/horse-only) -- Mount Olympus, Twin Peaks, Lone Peak, and
   Mount Timpanogos Wilderness. APPROXIMATE boundaries (traced from known canyon-road
   divides, not surveyed Forest Service data) but the underlying fact is real: these
   are federally designated wilderness, permanently closed to ATV/motorized travel.
4. Scouting Pins -- ranked candidate areas where real terrain data (aspect, landform,
   DWR crucial habitat overlap) and real computed hiking-time-from-access data
   intersect: good deer habitat that's genuinely hard for the crowd to reach on foot,
   cross-referenced against wilderness-area status. See each pin's description for
   specifics and reasoning.

WHAT THIS ISN'T: none of this shows you where a deer is standing right now. It shows
where the real data says good October habitat coincides with country that's hard to
reach and (mostly) legally closed to ATVs. Ground-truth with glassing and boots.
Verify current MVUM/seasonal closures before relying on any access assumption.

October mule deer behavior (general knowledge, not unit-specific data): by early
October mature bucks are typically solitary or in small groups, holding tight in
timber, not the big bachelor groups of August. Movement is minimal during the day --
glass timber edges and meadow edges at first and last light, still-hunt through timber
midday. Buck quality tends to increase with elevation and roadless distance. Late
October (pre-rut staging), start weighting travel corridors between summer and winter
range more heavily.</description>
